2.33.m:
Upon seeing a second adverse omen, however, he should re-enter his house.
Now I shall speak of the desired, auspicious omens, O sinless one:
White flowers, the foremost ones, and likewise a full water-jar,
aquatic beings, fish, meat, and fish, O descendant of Bhṛgu;
cows, horses, elephants, and a single tethered animal;
gods, friends, brahmins, and a blazing fire;
fortunate courtesans, cow dung blessed by ancient teachers,
gold, silver, copper, and likewise all kinds of gems;
medicinal herbs, O omniscient one, as well as sweet flag and white mustard;
a palanquin carried by men, and likewise an auspicious seat;
a sword, an umbrella, a banner, earth, and weapons;
all the insignia of royalty, and a corpse without weeping;
ghee, curds, milk, and various kinds of fruits;
a svastika, a vardhamāna, a nandyāvarta, together with the Kaustubha gem;

rivers depicted in paintings, and other auspicious things;
and principal unbroken grains of rice, and a mirror;
collyrium, yellow orpiment, ornament, and honey;
a conch shell, sugarcane, sweetmeats, and pleasant utterances;
the deep and charming opening sound of musical instruments;
and the notes gāndhāra, ṣaḍja, and ṛṣabha are recommended on a journey.
A wind full of gravel, harsh, blowing from the cardinal points,
adverse, and blowing low is to be known as fear-causing, O twice-born.
Favorable, gentle, smooth, and pleasant to the touch, it brings happiness.
Bears, harsh-sounding creatures, rhinoceroses, and carnivorous beasts are condemned.
Dense, glossy clouds resembling the trumpeting of elephants are auspicious;
a lightning flash moving favorably is praised, and likewise the rainbow of Śakra.
Torrents of yellow rain should be known as inauspicious;
planets moving favorably are praised, especially the lord of the direction.

2.34.m:
At the time of birth, from the place where the Sun is situated, in the third, sixth, tenth, and eleventh; from Mars's place, in the first, second, fourth, seventh, eighth, ninth, tenth, and eleventh; from Mercury, in the third, fifth, sixth, ninth, tenth, eleventh, and twelfth; from Jupiter, in the fifth, sixth, ninth, and eleventh; from Venus, in the sixth, seventh, and twelfth; from Saturn, in the first, second, fourth, seventh, eighth, ninth, tenth, and eleventh; from the ascendant, in the third, fourth, sixth, tenth, eleventh, and twelfth; [for the Moon] from the Sun's place, in the third, seventh, eighth, tenth, and eleventh; from its own, in the first, third, sixth, seventh, tenth, and eleventh; from Venus, in the third, fourth, fifth, seventh, ninth, and eleventh; for Mars, from the Sun, in the third, fifth, sixth, tenth, and eleventh; from its own, in the first, second, fourth, seventh, eighth, tenth, and eleventh; from Mercury, in the third, fifth, sixth, tenth, eleventh, and twelfth; from Venus, in the sixth, eighth, eleventh, and twelfth; from Saturn, in the first, fourth, seventh, eighth, tenth, and eleventh; from the ascendant, in the first, third, sixth, tenth, and eleventh; for Mercury, from the Sun, in the fifth, sixth, eighth, ninth, and eleventh; from the Moon, in the second, fourth, sixth, eighth, tenth, and eleventh; from Mars, in the first, second, fourth, seventh, eighth, ninth, and eleventh; from its own, in the first, third, fifth, sixth, ninth, eleventh, and twelfth, [it is] auspicious;
from Jupiter, in the sixth, eighth, eleventh, and twelfth, [it is] auspicious;
from Venus, in the first, third, fourth, fifth, eighth, ninth, and eleventh; from Saturn, in the first, second, fourth, seventh, eighth, ninth, tenth, and eleventh; from the ascendant, in the first, second, fourth, sixth, eighth, tenth, and eleventh. Jupiter [is auspicious] from the Sun in the first, second, third, fourth, seventh, eighth, tenth, and eleventh; from the ninth (dharma), in the second, fifth, seventh, ninth, and eleventh; from Mars, in the first, second, third, fourth, seventh, eighth, tenth, and eleventh; from Mercury, in the first, second, fourth, fifth, sixth, seventh, tenth, and eleventh; from Jupiter, in the first, second, third, fourth, seventh, eighth, tenth, and eleventh;
